{"ts":1792013735857,"kind":"said","id":"msg_011Cg2rBts1o3WnxWhZ8pcxj","text":"I wrote 12 tests in `tests/acceptance.part3.test.tsx` covering all ten criteria. I haven't seen any of them pass against a real implementation, because the app doesn't have one yet.\n\nThe file type-checks with `npx tsc --noEmit`, and I ran it twice. Every test fails today on an assertion or a failed lookup (for example \"no feeding row\", \"history rows missing\", `'142 d'` not matching 100). None crash in set-up or while rendering. The containers for S-2 and S-3 still just show the approved sample data, with no API calls. My first run showed AC-17.1 passing against that sample data, so I changed the feeding quantities to values the sample doesn't contain (6,360 planned, 6,075 delivered, −285 variance).\n\n**What each test checks**\n- **AC-17.1, AC-17.2:** After a feeding is saved on `/feed`, the row shows planned, actual and variance with an \"Adjust future plan\" action. Opening that action shows editable quantity fields plus the selected pen and ration.\n- **AC-18.1, AC-18.2:** Total weight recalculates as average × number weighed and there is no total input. 500 × 20 shows 10,000, and the saved record then appears in the weight history.\n- **AC-19.1:** Four dated measurements come back in shuffled order. The test checks each row's date, count, average, total, gain and notes, and that the order is monotonic in time.\n- **AC-20.1 (two tests):** One edits a weight record and one voids a feeding event. Each checks the revised metrics (and, for the void, the inventory balance) and that the original stays in history.\n- **AC-22.1, AC-22.2, AC-22.3:** Every returned metric is shown. The 100 days / 200 lb / ADG 2 / FCR 50 / cost 20 case is covered. Cost of gain is labelled as based on recorded feed costs.\n- **AC-23.1 (two tests):** After a weight save and after a feeding save, the returned metric values and suggestions appear with exactly one POST and no re-entry.\n\n**Assumptions**\n- **Selectors:** The tests assume the field labels and button names from the approved screens, and that the page's dialogs have the dialog role.\n- **API data:** The tests answer with generated handlers carrying my own rows, so the UI has to read from the generated client. There is no endpoint that lists feeding events, so the feeding tests record one through \"Feeding entry\" first.\n- **AC-22.3:** The API has no field for non-feed costs. The test therefore only proves the displayed basis (\"recorded feed costs\") and the returned value, not the calculation itself.\n\nI returned the screen id on the tests that render a screen: S-2 for the weight and metrics tests, S-3 for the feeding tests."}
